    SOUTHWESTERN PUBLIC SERVICE COMPANY’S EXPEDITED MOTION TO
      EXTEND DEADLINE TO FILE REBUTTAL TESTIMONY IN SUPPORT OF
                    COMPREHENSIVE STIPULATION

       In accordance with New Mexico Public Regulation Commission (“Commission”) Rule of

Procedure 1.2.2.12(A) NMAC, Southwestern Public Service Company (“SPS”) respectfully

moves to extend the deadline for any party filing rebuttal testimony in support of the

comprehensive stipulation in this case from July 9, 2026, to July 10, 2026, at 12:00 p.m. MT. In

support of this Motion, SPS states as follows:

       1.      On June 18, 2026, the Hearing Examiners issued an Order Revising Procedural

Deadlines (the “June 18 Order”).

       2.      The June 18 Order established deadlines for party positions and testimony on the

Comprehensive Stipulation filed in this proceeding by SPS, the New Mexico Department of Justice

(“NMDOJ”), New Mexico Large Customer Group (“NMLCG”), Occidental Permian Ltd.

(“OPL”), Louisiana Energy Services LLC (“LES”), Walmart, Inc. (“Walmart”), Federal Executive

Agencies (“FEA”), Targa Resources Corp. (“Targa”), Coalition for Clean Affordable Energy

(“CCAE”), and Prosperity Works (the “Stipulation”). Among other things, the June 18 Order set

the deadline for Staff to file testimony in opposition to the Stipulation for July 7, 2026, before


Page 1 of 3
 12:00 p.m. MT, and set the deadline to file rebuttal testimony in support of the Stipulation for July

9, 2026.

       3.      Staff filed testimony in opposition to the Stipulation from five witnesses on July 7,

2026. Two of Staff’s testimony was filed before the 12:00 p.m. MT deadline established in the

June 18 Order, one was filed at 1:00 p.m, one was filed at 1:36 p.m. and one was filed at

approximately 3:18 p.m. MT.

       4.      Given the scope of Staff’s testimony and the extremely short time between Staff’s

filing and the current July 9, 2026 close of business rebuttal deadline, SPS requests a short

extension of the rebuttal deadline until July 10, 2026, at 12:00 p.m. MT. The extension would

apply to any party filing rebuttal testimony in support of the Stipulation.

       5.      The requested extension is modest and will not affect the hearing on the Stipulation,

which is scheduled to begin on July 13, 2026. The extension will allow SPS, other parties

supporting the Stipulation, and any supporting witnesses a reasonable opportunity to review Staff’s

testimony and prepare responsive rebuttal testimony for the Hearing Examiners’ and

Commission’s consideration.

       6.      Good cause therefore exists to extend the deadline for any party filing rebuttal

testimony in support of the Stipulation to July 10, 2026, at 12:00 p.m. MT.

       7.      SPS has included a proposed Order Extending Deadlines, included as Exhibit A to

this Motion, as a convenience for the Co-Hearing Examiners.

       8.      Staff and the Intervenors were contacted regarding this motion and provided the

following positions: Staff – does not oppose; NMLCG – does not oppose; OPL – does not oppose;

Walmart – does not oppose; NMDOJ – does not oppose; Energy, Minerals, and Natural Resources




