  [Proposed] ORDER EXTENDING DEADLINE TO FILE REBUTTAL TESTIMONY IN
                        SUPPORT OF STIPULATION

        THIS MATTER comes before the Hearing Examiners upon Southwestern Public Service

Company’s Unopposed Motion to Extend Deadline to File Rebuttal Testimony in Support of

Stipulation (“Motion”), filed on July 8, 2026. Being duly informed, the Hearing Examiners FIND

and CONCLUDE:

        1.      On June 18, 2026, the Hearing Examiners issued an Order Revising Procedural

Deadlines.

        2.      The June 18 Order set the deadline for Staff to file testimony in opposition to the

stipulation for July 7, 2026, before 12:00 p.m. MT, and set the deadline to file rebuttal testimony in

support of the stipulation for July 9, 2026.

        3.      SPS requests a short extension of the rebuttal testimony deadline to July 10, 2026,

at 12:00 p.m. MT. The requested extension would apply to any party filing rebuttal testimony in

support of the Comprehensive Stipulation filed in this case.

        4.      The Motion is unopposed.
          4.      Having considered the Motion and the circumstances presented, the Hearing

Examiners find good cause to extend the deadline for any party filing rebuttal testimony in support

of the stipulation.

 IT IS THEREFORE ORDERED

         A.      The Motion is GRANTED.

         B.      The deadline for any party filing rebuttal testimony in support of the stipulation is

 extended to July 10, 2026, at 12:00 p.m. MT.

         C.      All other procedural requirements not inconsistent with this Order remain in effect.

 ISSUED under the Seal of the Commission at Santa Fe, New Mexico, on July ___, 2026.



